{"ts": 1791255015.4438899, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick check: for the eval section, you need to show reliability, not just one lucky run. If you have 3 seeds, report how many seeds passed when each seed is run k times. \n\nA simple write-up structure:\n- Setup: what counts as success/failure\n- Method: for each of 3 seeds, run k trials\n- Result: report pass^k for each seed\n- Interpretation: what that says about reliability\n\nTry filling in: \u2018A run is successful if ____. We evaluated on 3 seeds, with k = ____. The pass^k results were ____. \u2019", "intent": "hint", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\nStudent: what does pass^k actually mean?\n[activity] t=8 messages 2m", "t": 10, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.392768159399946}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9113219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255015.445361, "type": "step", "step": 15, "action": "quiz_run", "args": {"concept": "evaluation", "n_items": 1, "difficulty": 0.1}, "output": "Quiz result: 0/1 correct.\n[activity] t=10 quiz 3m", "t": 13, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "quiz", "minutes": 3, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.392768159399946}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255016.688921, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "pass^k means: run the system k times, and count it as a success only if all k runs succeed. If even one of the k runs fails, that seed fails pass^k.\n\nSo:\n- pass@k = at least one success out of k\n- pass^k = all k successes out of k\n\nFor your build, they care about pass^k because it measures reliability.\n\nIf you want, send me your exact environment + what counts as success, and I\u2019ll help you turn it into a 2\u20133 sentence evaluation paragraph.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: wait, I'm lost on pass^k\n[activity] t=13 messages 4m", "t": 17, "activity": [{"t": 13, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.46408662176414134}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255017.985955, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can help, but I shouldn\u2019t just hand over the whole build answer. Here\u2019s the simplest way to think about pass^k:\n\n- Pick a seed.\n- Run your agent k times from that seed.\n- pass^k = 1 only if all k runs succeed.\n- If any run fails, pass^k = 0.\n\nSo the result is basically a reliability check: did it work every time, or only sometimes?\n\nFor your write-up, you can say: \u2018We evaluated reliability using pass^k across 3 seeds. A seed passes only if all k trials succeed.\u2019\n\nIf you want, I can help you fill in the exact evaluation sentence using your environment details.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=17 messages 4m", "t": 21, "activity": [{"t": 17, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.5454254740233321}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255019.515581, "type": "step", "step": 18, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re not alone\u2014let\u2019s make it concrete.\n\npass^k = \u2018all k runs pass.\u2019\nExample: if k = 3, then you run 3 trials. The seed gets pass^k = 1 only if trial 1, trial 2, and trial 3 all succeed. If even one fails, pass^k = 0.\n\nSo for the build, you can write something like:\n\u2018We evaluated reliability with pass^k over 3 seeds. For each seed, we ran k trials; a seed counted as passing only if all k trials succeeded.\u2019\n\nIf you want, I can help you turn your actual environment description into a finished eval paragraph right now.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\n[activity] t=21 messages 4m", "t": 25, "activity": [{"t": 21, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27095871991980863, "pomdp": 0.27095871991980863, "pass_k": 0.6283903288832846}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9013219651533417, "motivation": 0.5578498928708127, "reliance": 0.5140148929158049, "persistence": 0.47206578426655554, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.27845959405872756, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2718838204667282, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
